<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51781" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθέψω</span></b> , fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εψήσω</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>boil down</i>, in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.555b
			</span></i>; of plants, <i>to be dried up</i> by the sun, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				7.5.2
			</span></i>; of a person, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡλίῳ
			-ψεῖσθαι</span> (sic) <i>to be broiled, swelter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				25
			</span></i>; of a river, to be <i>softened</i> (sweetened) by boiling,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.40
			</span></i>: 
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ψοντες ἑαυτούς</span>, by
			hot baths, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.185
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>soften, temper</i>, joined with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραΰνειν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				9.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>digest</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργύριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					795
				</span></i>
			 codd. (prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταπέψεις</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
